bench.py writes NOTHING to stdout on any path: its only progress output is
phase_log.txt, which it appends to after each phase, and its per-row output is
logs/<engine>_<config>_<instance>.{out,err}. grep 'print(' over
experiments/EXP-ICPERF-66fd51/code/bench.py returns no match.

This run's driver stream was NOT redirected to a file, so no captured stdout of
the driver exists and none is reconstructed here. That is a gap in the launch,
recorded rather than filled: RUN-ICPERF-305ca3 was launched with
> bench_stdout.log and this run was not.

The driver's actual output, in full, is:
  phase_log.txt                    -- 5 lines, one per phase, with wall seconds
